habendum.en:
n. That part of a deed which follows the part called the
   premises, and determines the extent of the interest or estate granted;
   -- so called because it begins with the word Habendum.

halidom.en:
n. Holiness; sanctity; sacred oath; sacred things; sanctuary;
   -- used chiefly in oaths.
n. Holy doom; the Last Day.

haloed.en:
imp. & p. p. of Halo
a. Surrounded with a halo; invested with an ideal glory;
   glorified.

heaves.en:
n. A disease of horses, characterized by difficult breathing,
   with heaving of the flank, wheezing, flatulency, and a peculiar cough;
   broken wind.

heterographic.en:
a. Employing the same letters to represent different
   sounds in different words or syllables; -- said of methods of spelling;
   as, the ordinary English orthography is heterographic.

homiletical.en:
a. Of or pertaining to familiar intercourse; social;
   affable; conversable; companionable.
a. Of or pertaining to homiletics; hortatory.

hoove.en:
n. A disease in cattle consisting in inflammation of the
   stomach by gas, ordinarily caused by eating too much green food;
   tympany; bloating.

huers.en:
plural of huer
n. One who cries out or gives an alarm; specifically, a balker;
   a conder. See Balker.

humoralism.en:
n. The state or quality of being humoral.
n. The doctrine that diseases proceed from the humors;
   humorism.
